WEBVTT

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:07.820
<i>We reeled it in.</i>

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.230
<i>We're neck and neck. We finally caught up.</i>

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:15.110
<i>Now all I have to do is never let go.</i>

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.430
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:55.400
<i>RIDE.11 Conclusion</i>

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:02.710
Now that they're on the downhill slope, 
Kaburagi and Danchiku are accelerating!

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:04.520
Sugimoto-kun and his brother 
are falling behind!

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:08.090
They're as good as you'd 
expect going downhill.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.680
What do you think will happen, Imaizumi?

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:12.800
They'll fall behind.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:13.400
What?

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:17.410
But they'll probably catch 
up on the next corner.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:24.160
<i>Who are these guys?</i>

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.980
Don't let go. Don't let go, Sadatoki.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.540
Let's go to the finish line.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:29.040
Yeah.

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:33.040
Team SS is a mixed team.

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:36.830
Since their fifteen members are 
determined through races,

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:41.950
they've probably never 
experienced that feeling...

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:45.350
Of riding with your friends.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.850
Currently, Kaburagi and 
Danchiku are stronger.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.980
But if Sugimoto has any chance at victory,

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:58.290
it's because their wavering spirits 
don't understand that feeling.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:02:59.490
<i>They're not good.</i>

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.450
<i>They're not supposed to be good.</i>

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:03.780
<i>So how did they catch up?</i>

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.410
<i>How are they neck and neck with us?</i>

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:10.540
Why are you riding in front of us?

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.630
Issa!

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:14.190
Don't waver!

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:15.770
Focus on the race!

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:18.010
You saw some guy pass you. That's all!

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:18.760
Danchiku...

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.990
Face forward and think only of winning.

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:23.510
We can do this. Don't worry.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:25.720
You're fast.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.510
You've practiced hard.

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:32.040
You've endured thousands 
of difficult moments.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.810
Aren't you going to race in the Inter-High?

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:37.570
So what's wrong with you?

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:39.110
Frolic more!

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:41.460
You're a genius, Kaburagi!

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.120
That did the trick.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.250
I'm fast? I'm a genius?

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.500
I know.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:56.920
I know that better than 
anyone else, Danchiku!

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.860
Yeah!

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:04.750
<i>Issa, I want to see you frolic like a child.</i>

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:08.390
<i>I want to see you refuse to 
shrink from strong opponents...</i>

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:11.300
<i>At this year's Inter-High.</i>

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.140
<i>That's why I'm riding with you.</i>

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.620
Switch with me, Issa. I'll pull.

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:17.120
The downhill is ending.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:20.920
I'll make sure you take first place!

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:23.450
It's the final spurt! Dig deep, Sadatoki!

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:23.990
Yeah!

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:30.040
<i>I'm not very good at goal sprints, 
but I'll overcome that weakness now.</i>

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.500
I don't have time for excuses.

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:37.630
At the bottom of the hill 
is Fumotogaoka Park.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:42.300
There's a short 200-meter climb from there.

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:46.640
It's the final goal sprint 
of the first-year race!

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:49.180
Danchiku-kun's in front!

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:52.770
Kaburagi-kun's behind him! 
They're going for the one-two finish!

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.480
Sadatoki's falling back!

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:59.100
We're going to the Inter-High, Danchiku!

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:00.880
We'll finish first and second!

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:07.270
From behind Danchiku, who was 
pulling with all his strength...

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:08.950
Go, Issa!

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:11.260
The Kaburagi Super Express 
is leaving the station!

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:12.910
Follow me, Danchiku!

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:16.290
It's ours. It's perfect.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:19.920
We're going to make 
Sohoku High School stronger.

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:23.590
Come, Danchiku! It's just us now!

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:25.050
Yeah!

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:30.580
Pedal, Issa! Don't worry about me!

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:31.880
Pedal!

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:35.190
Sugimoto passed him without 
any help from Sadatoki!

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:36.480
It's a long sprint.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:37.600
Sugimoto-kun.

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:40.630
<i>Your strength is long rides.</i>

00:05:41.390 --> 00:05:45.820
<i>Sugimoto, are you making your 
last spurt a long sprint, too?</i>

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:51.240
Sorry I couldn't help 
you in the end, Brother.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.760
<i>Thank you, Sadatoki.</i>

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:57.960
<i>If you hadn't pulled for me, I wouldn't 
have caught up to them on Minegayama.</i>

00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:00.750
<i>Thank you, Imaizumi.</i>

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:05.630
<i>If you hadn't pushed my back then,
I would've given up.</i>

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:08.740
<i>I haven't done a single thing.</i>

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:10.720
<i>Not a single thing.</i>

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:11.800
<i>So...</i>

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:15.190
Sugimoto!

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:16.290
He caught up!

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:18.700
You can't be serious!

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.650
Only forty meters left!

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:29.950
<i>I never realized how difficult it would be 
to prove I'm the fastest man in this race.</i>

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:31.410
Twenty meters left!

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:33.280
<i>Who the hell is this guy?</i>

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:35.040
<i>He should just fall back already.</i>

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:36.860
<i>How long will he endure?</i>

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:38.250
<i>Until we reach that line?</i>

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:39.210
Ten!

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:41.710
It's the goal. The finish line.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:45.810
I'll throw everything away if 
it means I'll reach it first!

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:50.460
No way! I'm the man who will 
surpass Onoda Sakamichi!

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:51.970
I'm going to be the sixth...

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:56.310
The sixth man!

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:02.350
Yeah!

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:11.650
Sugimoto-kun!

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:13.200
Are you okay, Sugimoto?

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:16.170
I felt it.

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:20.830
I was looking down when I crossed 
the finish line, so I couldn't tell.

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:23.790
But I...

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:26.250
I won.

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:30.920
I took first, right?

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:36.260
<i>He didn't hear Kaburagi yell.</i>

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:42.400
I did it! I'm going to the Inter-High!

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:44.500
I did it! I did it!

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:46.670
I did it!

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:48.610
Sugimoto.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:51.740
You did your best.

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:53.250
I did it.

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:57.580
I did it, Imaizumi. Thank you.

00:07:57.890 --> 00:07:59.580
Thank you, thank you.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:01.900
Words can't express how grateful I am.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:07.130
Huh?

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:11.050
Why do you all look so uneasy?

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:14.910
Is it because you don't want 
me to be the sixth man?

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:17.140
Don't worry. I can do it.

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:21.100
I, Sugimoto Terufumi,
will become even stronger.

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:39.200
We did it.

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:52.450
I see.

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:57.370
I wasn't first.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:09:01.030
B-But you were amazing.

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:02.910
Sugimoto-kun, you were amazing.

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:03.680
It's true.

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:06.120
You rode really well.

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:09.650
I was shouting when you caught up at the end.

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:11.230
Seriously.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:19.060
That was close. Second, huh?

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:21.870
That was truly close.

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:24.980
I almost had it.

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:28.520
Even I was confused.

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:31.510
Sorry, guys. Did I get your hopes up?

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:34.280
Sorry, sorry.

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:37.410
Teshima-san, Sugimoto-kun did his best.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:39.970
He tried really, really hard.

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:41.560
So, uh...

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:47.770
Why don't we wait until the training camp
 to decide the Inter-High team?

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:49.520
Until the training camp?

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:51.570
Last year, Kinjou-san ultimately decided—

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:52.980
Onoda...

00:09:56.400 --> 00:10:01.400
I was in this race with a different intention.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.160
Sugimoto-kun...

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:09.640
Teshima-san gave me a chance 
to ride in this race.

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:14.000
His condition was that I take first.

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:18.400
It was my last chance.

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:23.260
Ultimately, though, there is no next time.

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:26.680
I couldn't do anything.

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:30.770
Sugimoto...

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:34.330
You worked diligently every day.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:38.770
You're the only one who kept up 
with their initial acceleration.

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:41.410
You're the one who followed 
Sadatoki through the mountains

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:43.490
and caught up to them again.

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:46.750
During the final downhill 
sprint to the finish line,

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:50.030
it wasn't because of anyone else's 
strength or thanks to anyone else.

00:10:50.030 --> 00:10:51.420
You're the one who was riding.

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:55.500
Be proud. You had the 
strongest ride in this race.

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:58.370
Thanks, Imaizumi.

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:03.370
Sorry I couldn't win after all the advice you gave me.

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:07.350
I'm going to go cool down.

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.230
Brother...

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:19.830
<i>Sugimoto, I don't care if you win or 
lose as long as the team gets stronger.</i>

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:22.860
<i>Or so I thought, but...</i>

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:27.620
<i>During the final sprint, 
I was hoping you'd win.</i>

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:34.750
<i>I'm tired. I'm exhausted.</i>

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:36.600
<i>I got second.</i>

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:39.590
<i>I did everything I could.</i>

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:43.660
<i>I did everything I could!</i>

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.880
That was an impressive victory, Kaburagi.

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:54.650
Thanks.

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:59.770
But since Danchiku placed third, you didn't 
fulfill our agreement that a one-two finish

00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:02.320
meant both of you could become members.

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:04.990
Will you ride alone?

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:06.160
Yes, sir.

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:09.240
Good, Issa.

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:12.710
Get stronger.

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:13.400
Yes, sir.

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:16.700
It's nearly time.

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:17.460
Yeah.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:23.200
These are the Inter-High jerseys 
passed down to us from our seniors.

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:27.130
Winner of the first-year race, Kaburagi Issa.

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:27.680
Yes, sir.

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:37.900
You'll be wearing this. Take it.

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:39.780
Yes, sir.

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:42.340
They're here.

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:44.970
Vying for a consecutive victory...

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:47.920
The six members of the new 
Sohoku High School team.

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:53.150
I did it, I did it!

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.610
I did it!

00:12:56.410 --> 00:13:01.360
Naturally, I intended to become a member, 
but now that I am one, I'm ecstatic.

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:04.260
I tried on my jersey a 
bunch of times yesterday.

00:13:04.580 --> 00:13:07.640
Keep it down. Everyone will hear you.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:10.670
Listen to this! I'm going 
to be in the Inter-High!

00:13:10.670 --> 00:13:12.330
He's shouting even louder?

00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:14.130
As one of the champions,

00:13:14.130 --> 00:13:17.650
I'll lead Sohoku High School to 
our second consecutive victory.

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:20.980
Thank you!

00:13:21.870 --> 00:13:27.620
<i>He was strong. If the finish line had 
been five meters closer, I would've lost.</i>

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:30.410
<i>I seriously respect him.</i>

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:44.380
Push Imaizumi's back.

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:45.580
What?

00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:48.230
In my place.

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:52.430
Yes, sir!

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:58.270
<i>I understand the weight of riding in the 
Inter-High with this jersey, Sugimoto-san.</i>

00:13:58.910 --> 00:14:01.020
<i>Let's do this.</i>

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:03.720
Excuse me...

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:04.440
Yes?

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:06.440
Who is he?

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:11.040
Are you Onoda-san from the bicycle club?

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:12.440
Th-The national champion?

00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:13.460
Y-Yes.

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:15.750
How does it feel to be number one?

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:17.920
Uh, well...

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.810
Are your glasses for camouflage?

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:21.000
I'm here to see Kaburagi-kun...

00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:21.000
Can we take a picture?

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:22.290
Yeah!

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.210
Thank you!

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:28.090
No, wait. Could you please 
get Kaburagi-kun for me?

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:31.930
No, will you? I have a message for 
him from our captain, Teshima-san.

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:34.870
Stand. Bow.

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:41.330
<i>Just being in another grade's 
classroom makes me nervous.</i>

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:42.440
<i>But the upperclassmen...</i>

00:14:43.220 --> 00:14:44.730
Is Onoda here?

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:45.570
Yes, sir.

00:14:46.210 --> 00:14:48.190
<i>They didn't have a problem with it.</i>

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:51.930
<i>Being someone's senior is hard.</i>

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:00.010
Did you finish your report?

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:00.670
<b>Younan University</b>

00:15:00.010 --> 00:15:00.670
Yeah.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:02.880
What? What the hell is this?

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:06.130
<b>Notice

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:06.130
I rushed here, too. First period is canceled?

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:10.270
This college campus is too big.

00:15:10.270 --> 00:15:13.140
They should make it more
 compact so I don't get so tired.

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:16.430
I didn't think I'd get 
into a school this good.

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:20.190
Must've been my wild instincts at work.

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:26.230
Anyway, college is a tough place.

00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:29.890
I have some time before second period.

00:15:29.890 --> 00:15:31.450
Guess I'll go to the club room.

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:36.410
Since they have all kinds of clubs,
I should do something.

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:45.560
But I always end up here.

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:49.050
<b>Younan
University
Bicycle
Racing
Club</b>

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:47.880
First-year Arakita coming through.

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:55.720
I wasn't expecting to end up on 
the same team as you...

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:57.400
Kinjou.

00:15:57.400 --> 00:16:01.560
What are you mumbling about, Arakita?

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:04.800
Did you go to class because you 
didn't know it was canceled?

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:07.650
Shut up. And if you knew, 
you should've emailed me.

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:09.440
I don't have your address.

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:10.870
It's this.

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:12.870
A-K-I...

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:14.820
What's "Aki-chan"?

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:18.200
Shut up. It's my family's dog.

00:16:20.530 --> 00:16:24.960
What're you going to do about the next 
inter-school race? We're eligible.

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:28.820
Fuku-chan and Shinkai are coming to the race.

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:32.090
Meisou University's bike club is strong.

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:34.050
You think we'll win?

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:36.280
If we're in it, we'd better.

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:38.970
Interesting.

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:43.520
Let's show them the power 
of Younan University.

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:47.170
We're a really mismatched duo, though.

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:49.270
Maybe not.

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:56.070
Anyway, did you hear? This year's 
Inter-High is going to be on that slope.

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:57.920
That slope, huh?

00:16:57.920 --> 00:17:00.050
I'm glad it wasn't last year.

00:17:00.050 --> 00:17:02.080
Climbing that slope is exhausting.

00:17:02.970 --> 00:17:04.780
How do you think Sohoku High School will do?

00:17:04.780 --> 00:17:07.580
They've already picked out 
all six of their members.

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:08.960
That was quick.

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:11.940
Captain Teshima probably intends 
to use that time to increase

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:13.800
the team's strength as a whole.

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:18.850
That Teshima guy's pretty smart.

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:23.100
But I heard Izumida's been putting Hakone
Academy High School through hellish training.

00:17:24.030 --> 00:17:25.640
Sounds tough.

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:31.900
Since everyone's moved up a year, 
then that oddball—no, Onoda-chan...

00:17:32.620 --> 00:17:35.110
Is he a second-year now?

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:40.580
You sound like a tire going flat.

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:42.350
You got the sniffles, Onoda-kun?

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:43.580
Y-Yeah.

00:17:46.840 --> 00:17:48.820
Maybe someone's talking about me.

00:17:48.820 --> 00:17:50.880
<i>How undignified.</i>

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:54.420
Kaburagi-kun!

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:58.820
I went to your classroom this 
morning, but I missed you. Today—

00:17:58.820 --> 00:18:00.820
I heard from Teshima-san.

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:03.010
We're doing individual training, right?

00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:05.350
Great.

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:09.440
I went during lunch, too, 
but you weren't there.

00:18:10.140 --> 00:18:12.450
You'll be practicing one-on-one with Onoda.

00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:13.900
Learn all you can from him.

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:15.950
The practice follows a race format.

00:18:15.950 --> 00:18:20.470
The course is simple, running from the 
front gate and up the rear gate slope.

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:22.120
If you see an opening, pass him.

00:18:22.730 --> 00:18:25.270
Wh-Where did you go for lunch?

00:18:25.270 --> 00:18:28.390
You could've left a message 
with one of my classmates

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:31.080
to come see you during the next break.

00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:35.290
I couldn't do that. 
I wanted to tell you directly.

00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:36.760
I'll listen to your orders.

00:18:37.150 --> 00:18:38.720
After all, I'm your junior.

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:41.550
Sorry. Are you mad?

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:42.750
I'd apologize.

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:43.670
Sorry.

00:18:43.670 --> 00:18:47.120
<i>He's mad. Why is he mad?</i>

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:50.190
Huh? Kaburagi-kun?

00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:52.940
Juniors are so difficult to handle.

00:18:53.680 --> 00:18:57.010
My classmates told me—damn it.

00:18:57.010 --> 00:18:58.860
That Onoda's pathetic.

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:02.620
That he's unreliable, scrawny, and weak.

00:19:03.210 --> 00:19:08.500
They made fun of me for looking up to him!

00:19:08.950 --> 00:19:10.080
Damn it!

00:19:10.410 --> 00:19:12.980
Can't he be a more dignified senior?

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:15.130
He's embarrassing me!

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:16.340
Sorry.

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:20.360
Onoda-san, when did you get there?

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:22.240
Crap! S-Sorry...

00:19:22.240 --> 00:19:23.970
Did you hear me talking to myself?

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:27.810
<i>I was riding all-out.</i>

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:32.810
Yeah, sorry. From around
"where my classmates told me."

00:19:33.300 --> 00:19:37.000
<i>He kept up with me from the beginning?</i>

00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:41.160
Sorry. I'm not much of a senior, am I?

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:45.120
But I intend to do my best for the team.

00:19:45.710 --> 00:19:49.800
<i>This is crazy. My whole body is shaking now.</i>

00:19:50.280 --> 00:19:53.830
<i>Are there lots of other guys 
like him at the Inter-High?</i>

00:19:54.550 --> 00:19:56.430
Excuse me, uh...

00:19:56.430 --> 00:19:59.510
C-Could you ride as hard as you can?

00:20:00.850 --> 00:20:03.810
Th-This practice is about 
riding as hard as we can.

00:20:03.810 --> 00:20:06.240
Of course I will. Right!

00:20:06.790 --> 00:20:08.010
Here I go.

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:10.140
Okay.

00:20:13.390 --> 00:20:15.490
He's fast. What is this?!

00:20:15.490 --> 00:20:16.650
Is this him really climbing?

00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:18.400
It took only a moment.

00:20:18.740 --> 00:20:20.430
<i>What's going on with this guy?</i>

00:20:20.430 --> 00:20:23.940
<i>This pressure's been flowing out 
of his whole body since he started.</i>

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:27.740
<i>I've never met someone so fast going uphill.</i>

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:33.790
<i>This guy who looked so small 
at school looks huge now.</i>

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:36.570
I can't beat him. I don't 
think I can beat him.

00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:39.130
Racing against him is totally 
different from watching him.

00:20:40.020 --> 00:20:44.130
This is his high-cadence climb. Amazing!

00:20:45.070 --> 00:20:46.210
Keep up.

00:20:46.210 --> 00:20:47.300
Yes, sir.

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:50.730
<i>You truly are amazing, Onoda Sakamichi-san.</i>

00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:58.260
You think Kaburagi's flustered around now?

00:20:58.260 --> 00:20:59.070
Probably.

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:03.850
Most people are when they experience 
Onoda's riding firsthand.

00:21:03.850 --> 00:21:05.700
He even smiles while he climbs.

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:11.830
But we need Kaburagi to get stronger.

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:13.830
And we have to as well.

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:17.830
The next Inter-High is 
being held on that slope.

00:21:18.550 --> 00:21:19.590
That slope?

00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:23.820
Japan's most famous and 
endless winding slope.

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:30.470
Through cedar-lined roads, World Heritage Site
Toushougu Shrine, and beyond.

00:21:24.470 --> 00:21:26.470
<b>Nikkou National Park</b>

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:33.020
The Nikkou Irohazaka.

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:38.020
Among cyclists, it's known as
"The Sprinter Killer."

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:41.020
Its highest point is
1,840 meters above sea level.

00:21:41.830 --> 00:21:45.920
It's literally twice the size of last 
year's Hakone Mountain.

00:23:17.690 --> 00:23:19.820
Want to go for a short 
ride before second period?

00:23:19.820 --> 00:23:22.270
Not like I've got anything better to do.

00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:30.090
Kinjou...

00:23:33.590 --> 00:23:35.670
These aren't bad.

00:23:36.240 --> 00:23:39.930
<i>NEXT RIDE  Trouble!</i>

00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:44.940
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.
